    "https://www.saumag.edu/human-resources/2026/10/14/assistant-professor-of-educational-leadership-2/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Educational Leadership",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Educational Leadership | Human Resources | Southern Arkansas University Skip to main content Quick Links Calendar Directory mySAU Email: Student | Faculty Blackboard Course Schedule Library Give Tour Apply About Administration Accreditations Continuous Quality Improvement Consumer Information Financial Services Institutional Research Student Complaint Form Human Resources Mission and Vision Mulerider Mascot News Campus Map Faculty/Staff Resources Center for Excellence in Teaching & Learning Online Learning Physical Plant Request Staff Email Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Concurrent Enrollment Graduate Admissions International Admissions Tuition and Fees Cost Calculator Scholarships Financial Aid Orientation (BAM) Academics Colleges & Departments Business Education & Human Performance Liberal & Performing Arts Science & Engineering Honors Graduate Studies Majors and Degrees General Education Professional License Disclosure Academic Calendar Catalogs Resources Academic Advising Bookstore Magale Library Registrar Student Support Services Writing Center Online Learning Blackboard mySAU Course Schedules LiveText Student Email Final Exam Schedule Campus Life Students Club Sports Greek Life Let’s Talk Webcast Student Conduct Student Handbook Track the Ride Housing Application Costs Amenities Housing Options What to Bring Facilities Bookstore Campus Dining Campus Map Mulerider Activity Center Reynolds Center Story Arena Facilities Rental Physical Plant Request Mulerider Express Career Services Counseling Center University Health Services Athletics Alumni & Friends Alumni Association Office of Development Foundation The Stater Magazine A-Z Index Calendar Give Directory Apply Now Office of Human Resources About New Hires New Employee Orientation Policies Jobs Adminstrative Positions Faculty Positions Staff Positions Part-time Forms Whole Health Holiday Schedule Summer Staff Schedule Staff Awards Spirit of SAU Awards Valuing People Awards Whitehead Staff Excellence Awards Contact You are here: Home / Employment Opportunities / Assistant Professor of Educational Leadership Assistant Professor of Educational Leadership Southern Arkansas University invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor of Educational Leadership in the College of Education and Human Performance beginning Spring 2027 or Fall 2027. This is a face-to-face, on-campus position located in Magnolia, Arkansas. The faculty member will serve in the fully online Master of Education in Educational Leadership in Administration and Supervision (EDAS) program. SAU is a public regional institution with a total enrollment of approximately 4,700 undergraduate and graduate students and more than 350 faculty and staff. Our campus is located in Magnolia, a city of 11,000 in rural southwest Arkansas, approximately 50 miles east of Texarkana and 140 miles southwest of Little Rock. SAU is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. More information is available at www.saumag.edu . Duties: serve as Director of the Educational Leadership in Administration and Supervision program; develop and teach online courses; supervise EDAS adjunct instructors; participate in program accreditation, assessment, reporting, and continuous improvement activities; provide committee service and leadership; advise candidates toward successful program completion; demonstrate an optimistic, entrepreneurial outlook; collaborate with professionals from P–12 educational settings; develop and maintain scholarly activity; participate in opportunities to recruit, mentor, and retain students; and perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications: must have earned an Ed.D. or Ph.D. in Educational Leadership or a closely related field and professional experience as a K–12 administrator; must also demonstrate a commitment to the profession through P–12 teaching and leadership experience; effective oral and written communication skills; experience teaching graduate-level online courses and advising candidates; experience with accreditation, assessment, data analysis, and continuous improvement processes; working knowledge of AAQEP accreditation processes; experience with curriculum mapping and program revision. Preferred qualifications include a professional record of excellence, including scholarly publications. All SAU faculty and staff demonstrate a commitment to valuing all members of the SAU community, excellence in interpersonal interactions, and effective collaboration with colleagues. Joining the SAU family requires a commitment to our culture of Continuous Quality Improvement. Interested candidates should submit a detailed cover letter addressing the duties and qualifications; a current curriculum vitae; and the names, addresses, email addresses, and telephone numbers of three references who may be contacted. Application materials may be emailed to HR@saumag.edu or mailed to the Office of Human Resources, Southern Arkansas University, 100 E. University, MSC 9288, Magnolia, AR 71754-9288. Applicants must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the United States. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Review of applications will begin October 1, 2026. References other than those listed by the applicant may be contacted. EEO. Posted: October 14, 2026 Apply Online Contact Us Office of Human Resources 100 E. University OVR 115 Magnolia, AR 71753 Office (870) 235-4008 Fax (870) 235-5050 Staff Tammy  Sims Tammy  Sims Human Resources Manager Roger Giles Roger Giles Vice President for Administration & General Counsel Micah Williams Micah Williams Administrative Support Specialist Jennifer Richardson Jennifer Richardson Administrative Specialist III Important Links Fringe Benefits Brochure Payroll & Employee Benefits Health Insurance Plan Document Health Insurance Summary of Benefits and Coverage ABCBS - Machine-Readable Files SAU Tech Employment O